# Upstream Omarchy migrations this profile WANTS to run.
#
# The server profile does not run upstream migrations by default. Every
# migration shipped by the omarchy-server package is marked as already applied
# for root at install time and again on every package upgrade, by
# `omarchy-server-migration-seed` (run from the package's post_install /
# post_upgrade scriptlet). The reasoning is in that command's header and in
# docs/security-updates.md, "Upstream migrations on a server": migrations are
# written to carry a desktop session forward, a server profile ships current,
# they run under `bash -euo pipefail` inside an unattended update as root, and
# v4.0.2 shipped one that disabled sshd on a machine reachable only over ssh.
#
# This file is the way back in. One migration id per line -- the file name
# under /usr/share/omarchy/migrations, with or without the .sh suffix. Anything
# listed here is left UNMARKED, so it stays pending and the next
# `omarchy-migrate` runs it exactly as upstream intended.
#
#   1788124236
#   1788124236.sh     the same thing
#
# Blank lines and everything after a `#` are ignored.
#
# Adding an id here does not un-mark a migration that was already marked on a
# machine: a marker means the machine is past it, and un-marking would re-run a
# migration against a system that already moved on. Delete the marker under
# /root/.local/state/omarchy/migrations by hand to replay one deliberately.
#
# The list is reviewed on every upstream bump; see docs/maintenance.md.
#
# Empty on purpose: no upstream migration has been opted into yet.
